From bfbce8be4cc6f950057d049c18a12d4a78b4791f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 18:09:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 243/250] fix(u2b): declare the int8 envelope as a measured
 snapshot; gate proven-bound consumers

Round 2 after verify-0042-u2b refuted the revised measured envelope
(16696->75 > 56, 133144->841 > 457, alternate family 924 > 457).

- manifest: deviation_bound_kind=measured_snapshot, deviation_bound_available
  =false, no deviation_bound_by_k; measured_deviation_by_k aggregates the
  internal scan with the independent seeds-1-200 scans; measurement_scope
  carries the external observations and observations_are_not_a_bound; an
  explicit upper_bound block records status=not_provided and why (the pinned
  zen4 kernel is not the documented chained-f32 model; the model bound 59 is
  refuted by 75; an order-agnostic bound exceeds the int32 headroom)
- policy: numeric.require_proven_deviation_bound=true rejects providers whose
  deviation_bound_kind is not proven (exact_contract_bound /
  analytic_f32_chain_upper_bound); the portable reference keeps its proven
  exact_contract_bound; structured reason proven_deviation_bound_unavailable
- plan/report validation: a measured-snapshot envelope must not carry
  deviation_bound_by_k; the kind is mandatory
- tests: policy gate (reject snapshot / keep portable / accept a synthetic
  analytic kind) and the verifier witnesses 75/841 replayed through the
  provider; contract behavior unchanged (K<=1024 bitwise, K>=133145 and -128
  fail-closed before the kernel)
- evidence scripts: envelope now emits measured observations only; new
  envelope-refutation scan; fail-closed script covers the policy gate
